From 64abb999228d26fe81195cc076e1ff0954c3c2d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: khibye <chani.ch7765@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 14:33:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(socket): stop self-sustaining reconnect storms after a
 backend hiccup

A short database (or Redis) stall under load turned into an outage that did
not end when the backend recovered:

1. get_socket_session_user() treated any exception, including a pool
   timeout, as an invalid token and disconnected the socket.
2. The client reconnected immediately on 'io server disconnect'.
3. Every reconnect re-fetched the whole sidebar (chats, pinned, folders).
4. Those requests kept the pool saturated, so the next connect's token
   check timed out again -> goto 1. The load was a product of the loop.

A second loop appeared after a mass "Sign out all devices": a socket with a
revoked token was accepted without a user, every heartbeat disconnected it,
the client reconnected and re-fetched -> 401 x3 per cycle, and the sign-out
path depended on a confirmation request that failed under load.

Server (backend/open_webui/socket/main.py):
- distinguish "could not verify" (SQLAlchemy/Redis/timeout errors, and
  get_auth()'s 503) from "invalid token": keep the socket on the former and
  retry on the next sweep; disconnect only on the latter
- connect(): refuse cleanly with ConnectionRefusedError('backend_unavailable')
  on a transient error, and with 'unauthorized' when a supplied token is
  invalid, instead of accepting an anonymous socket
- heartbeat: never disconnect anonymous sockets; do not re-verify against
  the DB (the sweep does); write user.last_active_at at most every
  HEARTBEAT_LAST_ACTIVE_WRITE_INTERVAL (300 s) instead of every 30 s
- periodic_socket_authentication(): jitter, SOCKET_REAUTH_INTERVAL env,
  each check bounded by SOCKET_REAUTH_CHECK_TIMEOUT (5 s), yield every 50
  sockets, warn on overrun
- user-join: return {error: 'backend_unavailable', retry: true}

Client:
- +layout.svelte: exponential backoff with jitter (1-30 s) before
  reconnecting after 'io server disconnect' or a refused handshake; on
  'unauthorized' clear the session and go to the login page; retry
  user-join with backoff; sibling tabs follow a sign-out (storage event)
- Sidebar.svelte: skip reconnect-triggered full refreshes within 15 s

Reproduced and verified with 20 browser tabs against a deliberately small
DB pool (PostgreSQL paused 45 s; Redis removed 60 s; all sessions revoked)
on v0.12.5, v0.13.3 and dev: unpatched, pool timeouts and reconnects
continued for the whole 6-minute observation; patched, none after the
trigger. Reproduction and reports:
https://github.com/khibye/ope-webui-version-tests
